  "notes": "The rebuilt Hàm Rồng bridge crosses the Mã River in two gray steel through-truss spans. A single track runs inside the braced trusses, with separate cantilevered roadways, slender steel guardrails, and one central concrete river pier. The source reproduces the rebuilt gray steel crossing visible in the exterior photographs. The truss dimensions, rail ties and surface details are photo-led approximations. The named rail way and paired roadway centerlines fix the signed alignment and extents. Standard terrain under-resolves the embankments and riverbed. Short modeled retaining approaches carry the narrow-gauge track to the sampled banks. Outside them, the viewer uses its generic rail ribbon and track spacing.",
